  "rationale": "The sources satisfy the requirement. I judged this from the supplied excerpts and ran no tests or extra searches.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `IndexPlan::find` in `src/index.rs` builds a detail path for every key in `definitions`. Examples are included because `definitions` holds all definition kinds. It also rejects detail pages that collide with existing chapters.\n- `IndexPlan::populate` in `src/index.rs` adds one table row per definition. Each row has the form `` [`name`](detail_href) (kind noun) `` plus the evidence state label. It then attaches one generated subchapter per definition under the index chapter. Loading evidence through `LoadedDetailEvidence::load` ties each page to the validation report.\n- `render_detail_page` in `src/index.rs` emits a `[Requirements index]` link and a `[View definition]` link. The definition link points at the anchored definition, using `definition.kind.anchor(name)`. The page body comes from `render_detail_sections`, which receives the evidence. That function's body is not in the inputs, so the findings behaviour rests on the test assertions below.\n- `DefinitionKind::badge` and `DefinitionKind::anchor` in `src/lib.rs` give examples the `habeas-example-<name>` anchor.\n- The badge rendering in `src/lib.rs` (about lines 298–310) turns the definition badge into an `<a href=…>` that points at the detail page when an index plan exists.\n- The reference rendering in `src/lib.rs` (about lines 366–380) links references to the target definition's anchored location.\n\n**Tests**\n- `index_lists_examples_and_links_their_detail_pages` in `src/index.rs` is annotated with `{test}` for `requirements.examples.index`. It sets up one valid requirement, one example with a non-passing evidence file (`rules.pending`), and one example with no evidence (`rules.missing`). It asserts that:\n  - The definition chapter's example badge has `id=\"habeas-example-rules.pending\"` and an `href` to `requirements-index/rules.pending.html`.\n  - The index lists both examples with the `(example)` kind marker and links to their detail pages.\n  - Each detail page is created as a subchapter and shows the example text.\n  - The pending page has a `[View definition](../rules.html#habeas-example-rules.pending)` link and shows its rationale.\n  - The missing page has a \"Validation findings\" section containing \"missing for example\".\n- The `{test}`-annotated index test around `src/index.rs` lines 880–930 asserts a `[Requirements index](../requirements-index.html)` back-link on detail pages and the \"Valid\" evidence state.\n- `examples_are_distinct_definitions_and_tests_link_to_them` in `src/lib.rs` asserts that references to an example link to `../requirements.html#habeas-example-requirements.something.foo`.\n- `valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` in `tests/outcomes.rs` is also annotated for `requirements.examples.index`. It checks end-to-end that the index and detail pages show the FIXME state.\n\n**Gaps**\n- The new example test does not itself assert the back-link to the index. That is covered by the other index test, which uses requirements, and the detail page template is shared across kinds.\n- The new example test also does not assert the state label text in the example rows. Evidence-state rendering is shared across kinds and covered elsewhere.\n- Invalid (as opposed to missing) example evidence is not tested separately. It uses the same findings path as missing evidence.\n\nNone of these is acknowledged as a FIXME, and none is material enough to count as a gap.",
